    <item>
      <title>1. Introduction</title>
      <link>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/nmtran/intro/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/nmtran/intro/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div id=&#34;outline-container-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;headline-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;Introduction&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-text-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-text-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;NM-TRAN stands for NONMEM Translator, a FORTRAN 90/95 library that&#xA;preprocesses user inputs before a NONMEM run. It converts them into&#xA;three things: a &lt;em&gt;NONMEM data set&lt;/em&gt;, a &lt;em&gt;NONMEM control stream&lt;/em&gt; &lt;sup class=&#34;footnote-reference&#34;&gt;&lt;a id=&#34;footnote-reference-1&#34; href=&#34;#footnote-1&#34;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, and needed subroutines.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-container-headline-2&#34; class=&#34;outline-3&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;headline-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;What it does&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-text-headline-2&#34; class=&#34;outline-text-3&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;NM-TRAN takes a flexible input data set and turns it into a proper&#xA;NONMEM data set. It also takes a user-friendly NM-TRAN control stream and translates it into a NONMEM control stream.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2. Data</title>
      <link>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/nmtran/data/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/nmtran/data/</guid>
      <description>&lt;link rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; href=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/katex.min.css&#34; /&gt;&lt;script defer src=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/katex.min.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;script defer src=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/auto-render.min.js&#34; onload=&#34;renderMathInElement(document.body, {&amp;#34;delimiters&amp;#34;:[{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;$$&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;$$&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:true},{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\(&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\)&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:false},{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\[&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\]&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:true}]});&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-container-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;headline-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;Data and event records&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-text-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-text-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Data are specified for NONMEM using &lt;em&gt;event records&lt;/em&gt; &lt;sup class=&#34;footnote-reference&#34;&gt;&lt;a id=&#34;footnote-reference-1&#34; href=&#34;#footnote-1&#34;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;.&#xA;They represent temporal events such as dose events,&#xA;observation events, and others such as the beginning&#xA;of a urine collection and a measured change in kidney function.&#xA;Data records (rows in the data file)&#xA;correspond to different events, and must be in the order of time.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;Data records also represent individuals, by grouping an individual&amp;#39;s records in contiguous&#xA;records with a same &lt;em&gt;ID&lt;/em&gt;. We refer to such a group an &lt;em&gt;individual record&lt;/em&gt;.&#xA;Data records in an individual record must be ordered in time.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
